<title>SOUTH AFRICA: NRB yr shr steady, div cut.</title>
<headline>NRB yr shr steady, div cut.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>		(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr (cts)</p>
<p>    - attrib		     20.7	     vs   20.6</p>
<p>    - fully diluted	    23.7	     vs   24.2</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		    5.0		vs   7.0</p>
<p>    Net income		   70.55	    vs   63.12</p>
<p>    Net interest income	45.43	    vs   36.90</p>
<p>    Other operating income   25.11	    vs   26.22</p>
<p>    Bad/doubtful debt charge 15.33	    vs   11.40</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			8.18	     vs   6.76</p>
<p>    Tax			    1.36 received  vs   0.76 paid</p>
<p>Div payable July 24</p>
<p>On register July 4</p>
<p>Full name: New Republic Bank Ltd (banks and other financial services)</p>
<p>NOTE - The group said the completion of a restructuring process had put the group in a strong financial position and was looking forward to growth off a low asset base.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
